Update the properties of a specified volume.

USAGE:
  scw instance volume update <volume-id ...> [arg=value ...]

EXAMPLES:
  Change the volume name
    scw instance volume update 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111 name=my-new-name

  Change the volume disk size (bytes)
    scw instance volume update 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111 size=60GB

  Change the volume name and disk size
    scw instance volume update 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111 name=a-new-name size=70GB

ARGS:
  volume-id         ID of the volume to update
  [name]            New name for the volume
  [tags.{index}]    New tags for the volume
  [size]            New size for the volume
  [zone=fr-par-1]   Zone to target. If none is passed will use default zone from the config (fr-par-1 | fr-par-2 | fr-par-3 | nl-ams-1 | nl-ams-2 | nl-ams-3 | pl-waw-1 | pl-waw-2 | pl-waw-3 | it-mil-1)

FLAGS:
  -h, --help[=true|false]                help for update
      --list-sub-commands[=true|false]   List all subcommands
  -w, --wait[=true|false]                wait until the volume is ready

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta[=true|false]         Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string             The path to the config file
  -D, --debug[=true|false]        Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers[=true|false]   Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string             Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string            The config profile to use
      --web[=true|false]          open console page for the current resource
